        "Description": [
            {
                "value": "This research project aims to investigate long-term population dynamics and trends in carabids with a special focus on the lowland beech forests of Schorfheide-Chorin Biosphere Reserve. The researchers work with continuous fine-scale time series data as well as with a larger-scale repeated survey. Other aspects of the project focus on the improvement of methods used to investigate trends in insect populations.",
                "qualifier": "researchDesign",
                "lang": "-"
            },
            {
                "value": "Data was collected in the course of teaching activities at Eberswalde University for Sustainable Development.",
                "qualifier": "note",
                "lang": "en"
            },
